From 2ca89289140d04fd15764a3fc9627e70d33ebe73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elsirion <elsirion@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:08:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(worktrees): allow a new worktree's .envrc with direnv

direnv keys its allow list by path and content, so every worktree Orca
creates starts with a blocked `.envrc` even when the same file is
trusted in the main checkout, and shells and agents in it run without
the project environment until someone runs `direnv allow`. Mirror what
workspacer-style tools do: after a successful local `git worktree add`,
run `direnv allow` on the checkout's `.envrc` when direnv is installed.

`--no-checkout` adds have no `.envrc` yet and WSL checkouts belong to
the distro's direnv, so both are skipped. A missing direnv is silent;
any other failure is a warning and never fails the create.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
